{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin","id":1034803,"title":"Entropy: Disambiguation (Sphere) ALSO: broken nomenclature, and the Ahl i Batin","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-19T13:00:18-08:00","id":1034803,"title":"Entropy: Disambiguation (Sphere) ALSO: broken nomenclature, and the Ahl i Batin","content":"I see that this Sphere is the least understood of all by people in general, so I thought maybe I could share some insights about it (and to gain insights too).<br /> <br /> Quick notes: (I'll expand later)<br /> 1- <i>Entropy</i>, as one of the Triad forces (Wyrm), has no relation with the <i>Entropy Sphere</i>, AT ALL<br /> 2- Entropy deals with <b>Fate</b>. Destiny. Not chance <i>per se</i>, and certanly, not <u>destruction</u>.<br /> 3- Levels 3-5 doesn't give <b>direct</b> control of their areas of action (matter, life, mind). It is <b>inderect</b> control.<br /> 4- The name of the sphere makes no sense, considering Mage Lore. First of all, the system of Spheres, althouth it is the way we deal with the game mechanics, is NOT consensus amongst the paradigms of the Traditions (in terms of interpretation, most Mages don't think about their powers in terms of Spheres, even if we, as players, must, for rules purposes). Instead, it's a system that were created by the <b>Hermetic Order</b>. Problem is: the word &quot;Entropy&quot; is a scientific physical denomination. It fits the Technocracy, perhaps even the Etherite or VA, but not the hermetics. It would be much more logical if it were named &quot;Fate Sphere&quot; or &quot;Destiny Sphere&quot;.<br /> 5- The ban on Entropy by the Batini makes no sense (I'll expand later). It would make more sense for the Celestial Chorus to ban it than the Batini (I'll also expand later)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T15:13:16-08:00","id":1034895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin#post1034803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2- Entropy deals with <b>Fate</b>. Destiny. Not chance <i>per se</i>, and certanly, not <u>destruction</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specialties: Fate, Fortune, <b>Decay</b>, Order, Chaos, <b>Necromancy</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Controlling the <b>energies of probability and</b> <u><b>decay</b></u>, an Entropy-schooled mage can manipulate random factors, observe and <b>influence flaws within a system</b>, tap into the energies of the Low Umbra, <b><u>induce</u> or remove <u>corruption</u></b>, and otherwise exert his Will through the inexorable process of mortality.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://31.media.tumblr.com/01b22b9517c58d493fa76e5dbec0269b/tumblr_msnag7B8of1su4cb8o1_500.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T15:42:22-08:00","id":1034904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin#post1034803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see that this Sphere is the least understood of all by people in general, so I thought maybe I could share some insights about it (and to gain insights too).<br /> <br /> Quick notes: (I'll expand later)<br /> 1- <i>Entropy</i>, as one of the Triad forces (Wyrm), has no relation with the <i>Entropy Sphere</i>, AT ALL<br /> 2- Entropy deals with <b>Fate</b>. Destiny. Not chance <i>per se</i>, and certanly, not <u>destruction</u>.<br /> 3- Levels 3-5 doesn't give <b>direct</b> control of their areas of action (matter, life, mind). It is <b>inderect</b> control.<br /> 4- The name of the sphere makes no sense, considering Mage Lore. First of all, the system of Spheres, althouth it is the way we deal with the game mechanics, is NOT consensus amongst the paradigms of the Traditions (in terms of interpretation, most Mages don't think about their powers in terms of Spheres, even if we, as players, must, for rules purposes). Instead, it's a system that were created by the <b>Hermetic Order</b>. Problem is: the word &quot;Entropy&quot; is a scientific physical denomination. It fits the Technocracy, perhaps even the Etherite or VA, but not the hermetics. It would be much more logical if it were named &quot;Fate Sphere&quot; or &quot;Destiny Sphere&quot;.<br /> 5- The ban on Entropy by the Batini makes no sense (I'll expand later). It would make more sense for the Celestial Chorus to ban it than the Batini (I'll also expand later)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. Not entirely correct. according to the Book of Madness, the Nephandi often emphasise use of the sphere of Entropy, and all members are encouraged to gain at least the first rank, and there is one group of nephandi, the Malfeans, who are effectively servants of the Wyrm (regardless of whether or not they think the Wyrm exists literally or just conceptually).<br /> <br /> 2. Again, not entierly. Fate, Chance, and Decay are all part of what the Entropy sphere encompases, and a lot of how these things manifest depends very heavily on paradigm.<br /> If you consider your life to be planed out from the start, then Entropy is the sphere of fate, shifting outcomes around and moving your path around.<br /> If you think there is no plan, that it's all just luck, then Entropy is the sphere of chance, being able to fix the odds in your favour, providing Fortune.<br /> <br /> It should be noted that there are whole sects of Euthanatos who devote themselves entirely to Chance based magic, rolling dice, flipping coins, shuffling cards, throwing rings and seeing where they land. For them, Entropy is all about the manipulation of chance, circumstance, and happenings.<br /> <br /> In addition, you may have the view that the only certainty in life is that all things fall apart. Real life physics has demonstrated that all things tend towards higher entropy. This means that all ordered systems will become increasingly disordered over time, until there is not distinguishing features of their being. Walls crumble to dust, Plants wilt and rot. People age and forget. Ideas evolve and become loss.<br /> The Entropy sphere is able to sense how far along things are towards their &quot;final fate&quot; as they were, and thus be used to determine how far from Order, or close to Chaos they are. Thus higher levels will give the mage the ability to affect order or chaos within a given system.<br /> <br /> 3. I'd agree with this. Expanding on it, I'd say this Sphere allows you to dictate the outcome, but the methods of achieving the outcome are out of your control without the use of other spheres.<br /> <br /> 4. If it makes you feel better, the Hermetics actually calls it &quot;<i>Ars Fati</i>&quot; and originally &quot;<i>Ars Fortunae</i>&quot;. But regardless of that, how do you know it wasn't the other way around? That the term Entropy originally came from a mystic source, and the Technocracy appropriated it, changed its definition to one which suited their own paradigm, and then revised history to make it seem as though that's how it always was?<br /> <br /> The Problem with calling it the &quot;Fate&quot; sphere is that not all mages believe in Fate. Similarly not calling it the &quot;Chance&quot; sphere is not all mages believe in Chance. Entropy, on the other hand, is a concept that most mages from the traditions should be able to understand and internalise in whatever way they see fit. Some as luck, some as fate, some as decay. It's a word which encompasses all these meanings, and is therefor much more useful for cross tradition discussion, which is the whole point of codifying the spheres this way in the first place.<br /> <br /> 5. I'm not all that knowledgable of the Batini, but if you're basing this on the assumptions you've made above (That Entropy is exclusively about fate, rather than chance or decay), then I think you may be coming to false conclusions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-19-2017, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T16:10:06-08:00","id":1034919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1034904#post1034904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition, you may have the view that the only certainty in life is that all things fall apart. Real life physics has demonstrated that all things tend towards higher entropy. This means that all ordered systems will become increasingly disordered over time, until there is not distinguishing features of their being. Walls crumble to dust, Plants wilt and rot. People age and forget. Ideas evolve and become loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold on cowboy, this is not quite true. The second law of thermodynamics states that a total entropy of an <i>isolated</i> system always either remains constant or goes up. What this <i>means</i> is that natural processes are not reversible. When you put a piece of cold bacon on a hot pan the heat will always go from the pan to the bacon, and never the other way around. Entropy doesn't concern itself with a destruction of a system, but rather with its change and use of energy. When a plant grows - that's increase in entropy as the plant takes energy from the system of plant and sun. And of course entropy doesn't apply at all to things like &quot;ideas&quot;, which are not physical objects with energy.<br /> <br /> There is also a concept of entropy in Informatics, but it's largely unrelated to physical entropy. Entropy in informatics is a measure of uncertainty about the contents of any given message.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T16:10:32-08:00","id":1034920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin#post1034803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see that this Sphere is the least understood of all by people in general,</div> </div> </div> </div>And you're apparently including the writers in that. I mean, I might agree that the Batini being unable to use Entropy is not great writing, but it's still a part of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T16:30:43-08:00","id":1034929,"title":"","content":"The OP makes a valid argument for what SHOULD be the case (and its the root Awakening went with the Fate Arcanum), but canonically as written Entropy absolutely governs decay and destruction as a force in its own right (and serves as a Sphere tax on what should be purely Spirit effects to deal with the dead/underworld).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T16:35:10-08:00","id":1034933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1034929#post1034929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The OP makes a valid argument for what SHOULD be the case (and its the root Awakening went with the Fate Arcanum), but canonically as written Entropy absolutely governs decay and destruction as a force in its own right (and serves as a Sphere tax on what should be purely Spirit effects to deal with the dead/underworld).</div> </div> </div> </div>You only need Entropy to visit the underworld. Anything you can do to spirits with Spirit, you can do with Wraiths with Spirit just as easily.<br /> If anything, using Entropy on Wraiths only creates bigger problems, and is thus a pretty bad idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T19:25:01-08:00","id":1035006,"title":"","content":"I've not seen as many people confused by Entropy for what it is as I have seen those that struggle to put it into action. And even then only at the lower ranks. From rank 3 and up it's pretty self explanatory, even to the new players I've dealt with.<br /> <br /> I've had far more players have trouble effectively use Spirit than I have Entropy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:03:18-08:00","id":1035317,"title":"","content":"Thank you all guys, it has been very insightful. Maybe I can buy another Arete level now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll try to counter argument a few of those points, just gimme a sec","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:37:12-08:00","id":1035336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1034895#post1034895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Originally posted by <b>M20</b><br /> Controlling the energies of probability and <b>decay</b>, an Entropy-schooled mage can manipulate random factors, observe and influence flaws within a system, tap into the energies of the Low Umbra, <b>induce or remove corruption</b>, and otherwise exert his Will through the inexorable process of mortality.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, I've just looked my 3ed (I don't have M20). <br /> <br /> <i>Mea Culpa</i><br /> <br /> That's however, a bit different from 3ed. So, it seems they emphasyzed that hole &quot;decay&quot; aspect.<br /> <br /> Still, to me, it looks like many people still have this association between Entropy (Sphere) = Wyrm. And that view seems to affect some of the writers too. That part of &quot;tap into the energies of the Low Umbra&quot; makes absolutely no sense at all... And yet, we must consider it cannon.<br /> <br /> To make a correlation between the Sphere of Entropy with the Wyrm would be the same as saying that the Spirit Sphere is tainted because I can use it to summon banes, make Fomori or take residence in the Abyss.<br /> <br /> It's absolutely nonsensical.<br /> <br /> I could just as easily say that Entropy is an Sphere connected to the Weaver - an Iteration X master in Entropy would have the most perfectly organized lab in the Tellurian, where everything would be absolutely precisely and predictable; even his very own movements would work sinchronized with the rest, and his bodily functions would have precise changes to match his lab (and vice versa - for example, he would always sleep 10:02 p.m. and awake EVERYDAY at 6:02 a.m., his robots would always prepare his bed at 9:56pm and clean it from 6:03am to 6:05 am, his main computer would always turn on at 10:09, which is exactly the moment that he finished cleaning the teeth and changing clothes, just 45 seconds before he sits on his chair to start his work, and so on).<br /> <br /> But I could also argue that Entropy is the Sphere of the Wyld; an excentric Mage with a Dinamic Essence m\u00e1ster in Entropy, could have the most chaotic sanctuum ever; completely random wings all the time, a lot of bells and other stuff that makes noise with the wind making a cacofonic profusion of sounds, all his research is written on the hundreds of thousands of paper pages always dancing around according to the wind - however, he has only to open his hand to grab EXACTLY the page that he needs at any moment, thousands of small insect-like creatures fly around, grabbing and dropping stuff around at what seems a totally random pattern, yet, if the Mage need his magikal dice, for example, one of those insects will drop them in his hands without him needing to ask... In fact, the WHOLE place adapt to the will and needs of the Mage, without him needing to ask - one of his many golems that keep the place will bump on a chair, throwing it under the Mage in the exactly same moment as he lets his body fall, even his coffe will be prepared by a series of random events and will be dropped on his table &quot;by luck&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, I refuse to make this inference that Entropy = Destruction/Decay, ergo, Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Its how you use the Sphere that will say if it is Patter/Entropy/Dynamism, not the Sphere itself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:12:47-08:00","id":1035367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1034904#post1034904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Not entirely correct. according to the Book of Madness, the Nephandi often emphasise use of the sphere of Entropy, and all members are encouraged to gain at least the first rank,</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because of their use of the Sphere rather than some &quot;corruptive&quot; intrinsical nature of it<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1034904#post1034904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and there is one group of nephandi, the Malfeans, who are effectively servants of the Wyrm (regardless of whether or not they think the Wyrm exists literally or just conceptually).</div> </div> </div> </div>It is suggested that their Malfean &quot;Dread Lords&quot; could be the Onceborn (and even Neverborn) spetral gods of the Oblivion in the Low Umbra, but it could also be the powerful Spirits that serves the Wyrm. Or it could be both. That will be up to the ST.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1034904#post1034904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Again, not entierly. Fate, Chance, and Decay are all part of what the Entropy sphere encompases, and a lot of how these things manifest depends very heavily on paradigm.<br /> If you consider your life to be planed out from the start, then Entropy is the sphere of fate, shifting outcomes around and moving your path around.<br /> If you think there is no plan, that it's all just luck, then Entropy is the sphere of chance, being able to fix the odds in your favour, providing Fortune.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, my bad. You're right, I think some spirit of confusion were playing tricks on my mind when I wrote. I wasn't been able to organize my own ideas when I were making the topic (Chaos took over).<br /> <br /> Yes, Fate, Chance, Order and Chaos (I made a mess, and forgot that Fate implies predestination, so it's the opposite of Chance). Better to say, in a scientific view point that everybody will understand, it deals with the Universal Chaos (I'm not dealing with paradigms in-game here, so lets forget about the game and think about real life physics work - for example, &quot;order&quot; isn't really a thing in physics: what we would call &quot;order&quot; is simply &quot;less Chaos&quot; - much like &quot;dark&quot; is just absence of light and not it's opposite analogy for Forces)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1034904#post1034904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be noted that there are whole sects of Euthanatos who devote themselves entirely to Chance based magic, rolling dice, flipping coins, shuffling cards, throwing rings and seeing where they land. For them, Entropy is all about the manipulation of chance, circumstance, and happenings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Already corrected above. Sorry again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1034904#post1034904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition, you may have the view that the only certainty in life is that all things fall apart. Real life physics has demonstrated that all things tend towards higher entropy. This means that all ordered systems will become increasingly disordered over time, until there is not distinguishing features of their being. Walls crumble to dust, Plants wilt and rot. People age and forget. Ideas evolve and become loss.<br /> The Entropy sphere is able to sense how far along things are towards their &amp;quot;final fate&amp;quot; as they were, and thus be used to determine how far from Order, or close to Chaos they are. Thus higher levels will give the mage the ability to affect order or chaos within a given system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't fully agree with that part, but Kammerer above already said it all<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1034904#post1034904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. If it makes you feel better, the Hermetics actually calls it &amp;quot;<i>Ars Fati</i>&amp;quot; and originally &amp;quot;<i>Ars Fortunae</i>&amp;quot;. But regardless of that, how do you know it wasn't the other way around? That the term Entropy originally came from a mystic source, and the Technocracy appropriated it, changed its definition to one which suited their own paradigm, and then revised history to make it seem as though that's how it always was?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what the hermetics say<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1034904#post1034904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with calling it the &amp;quot;Fate&amp;quot; sphere is that not all mages believe in Fate. Similarly not calling it the &amp;quot;Chance&amp;quot; sphere is not all mages believe in Chance. Entropy, on the other hand, is a concept that most mages from the traditions should be able to understand and internalise in whatever way they see fit. Some as luck, some as fate, some as decay. It's a word which encompasses all these meanings, and is therefor much more useful for cross tradition discussion, which is the whole point of codifying the spheres this way in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I may agree in parts that <i>maybe</i> this could help inter traditions discussions, the history of Mage dictates that all the system of the Sphere division were created by the Order of Hermes, and that many Traditions don't even use it AT ALL (but there is no other alternative anywhere else, nonetheless it's there)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1034904#post1034904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. I'm not all that knowledgable of the Batini, but if you're basing this on the assumptions you've made above (That Entropy is exclusively about fate, rather than chance or decay), then I think you may be coming to false conclusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Batini are all about BALANCE. In fact, they should be the best students of Entropy, because they could use it with great effect to RESTORE BALANCE TO THE WORLD.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Entropy should be anatema to the Celestial Chorus... Everything that is, comes from The One, and even that which could seem against The One, only is make his glory even more magnificent... Who do you think you are to interfere with The One's plans? Changing Fate is changing the &quot;God's Plan&quot;, and interfere with God's Plan is the WORSE of the sins...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:16:26-08:00","id":1035370,"title":"","content":"Why does the idea of Entropy tapping into the energies of the Lower Umbra not make sense? The Lower Umbra is where things end. The sphere of Entropy manipulates the the integrity of things, people, ideas, etc and can bring them to the end of their cycle. I feel it makes perfect sense. Just as the sphere of Mind can be tied to the High Umbra where ideas begin and Life is tied to the Middle Umbra where idea takes form Entropy is tied to the Lower Umbra where all things end. As for relating Entropy to the Wyrm I think its more of a hold over from Werewolf and how they see it, right or wrong. A Mage normally doesn't make this distinction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:16:30-08:00","id":1035371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1035336#post1035336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right, I've just looked my 3ed (I don't have M20).<br /> <br /> <i>Mea Culpa</i><br /> <br /> That's however, a bit different from 3ed. So, it seems they emphasyzed that hole &quot;decay&quot; aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look. If you are going to come here and educate us foolish mortals who can not comprehend the concept of Entropy as fully as your magnificent mind can, then you can at least read the goddamn book to make sure you do actually know what you are talking about. Because you know, I can post quotes from Revised book too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage Revised</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specialties: Chaos, <b>Dissolution</b>, Fate, Fortune, Order.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage Revised</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>All things dissolve eventually into haphazard components</b>, and similarly events form from disjointed, unconnected patterns. Whether in thermodynamic theory or metaphysical metaphor, <b>Entropy describes the simple fact that all things break down</b>, but that new states come from disorder.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage Revised</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In practical physical terms, <b>Entropy also relates an understanding of the breakdown of systems</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>------------------------------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1035336#post1035336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, to me, it looks like many people still have this association between Entropy (Sphere) = Wyrm. And that view seems to affect some of the writers too. That part of <b>&quot;tap into the energies of the Low Umbra&quot;</b><u><b>*</b></u> makes absolutely no sense at all... And yet, we must consider it cannon.<br /> <br /> To make a correlation between the Sphere of Entropy with the Wyrm would be the same as saying that the Spirit Sphere is tainted because I can use it to summon banes, make Fomori or take residence in the Abyss.<br /> <br /> It's absolutely nonsensical.<br /> <br /> I could just as easily say that Entropy is an Sphere connected to the Weaver - an Iteration X master in Entropy would have the most perfectly organized lab in the Tellurian, where everything would be absolutely precisely and predictable; even his very own movements would work sinchronized with the rest, and his bodily functions would have precise changes to match his lab (and vice versa - for example, he would always sleep 10:02 p.m. and awake EVERYDAY at 6:02 a.m., his robots would always prepare his bed at 9:56pm and clean it from 6:03am to 6:05 am, his main computer would always turn on at 10:09, which is exactly the moment that he finished cleaning the teeth and changing clothes, just 45 seconds before he sits on his chair to start his work, and so on).<br /> <br /> But I could also argue that Entropy is the Sphere of the Wyld; an excentric Mage with a Dinamic Essence m\u00e1ster in Entropy, could have the most chaotic sanctuum ever; completely random wings all the time, a lot of bells and other stuff that makes noise with the wind making a cacofonic profusion of sounds, all his research is written on the hundreds of thousands of paper pages always dancing around according to the wind - however, he has only to open his hand to grab EXACTLY the page that he needs at any moment, thousands of small insect-like creatures fly around, grabbing and dropping stuff around at what seems a totally random pattern, yet, if the Mage need his magikal dice, for example, one of those insects will drop them in his hands without him needing to ask... In fact, the WHOLE place adapt to the will and needs of the Mage, without him needing to ask - one of his many golems that keep the place will bump on a chair, throwing it under the Mage in the exactly same moment as he lets his body fall, even his coffe will be prepared by a series of random events and will be dropped on his table &quot;by luck&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, I refuse to make this inference that Entropy = Destruction/Decay, ergo, Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Its how you use the Sphere that will say if it is Patter/Entropy/Dynamism, not the Sphere itself</div> </div> </div> </div><b><u>*</u> </b>&quot;Low Umbra&quot; means Underworld.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20 &quot;Lower Umbra&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are all mortal. Magic gives us the means to stall death, even undo its effects for a short time. All things, however, die eventually: Gods, vampires, even ideas. And the Low Umbra is where dead things go when they pass beyond the Earthly plane.<br /> <br /> A living mage can enter the Shadowlands; magic gives us that much power, though at a fairly high cost. Beyond that entry, though, the Low Umbra remains mysterious, with many stories but very few conclusions other than the ultimate end of life itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>But other than that, I really don't know who you are arguing with. No one in this thread claimed that Entropy and Wyrm are related. No one anywhere has claimed that Entropy &quot;is tainted&quot;. I personally have never played with anyone who tried to hammer Werewolf mythology into Mage, but this can be chalked up to limited sample size. You are tilting at windmills mate. And you are being condescending while doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:21:51-08:00","id":1035375,"title":"","content":"Quote Karlgust:<br /> On the other hand, Entropy should be anatema to the Celestial Chorus... Everything that is, comes from The One, and even that which could seem against The One, only is make his glory even more magnificent... Who do you think you are to interfere with The One's plans? Changing Fate is changing the &quot;God's Plan&quot;, and interfere with God's Plan is the WORSE of the sins...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This of course assumes that a Mage that manipulates the Threads of Fate for himself or another wasn't doing so because it WAS his fate to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:53:55-08:00","id":1035388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1035370#post1035370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does the idea of Entropy tapping into the energies of the Lower Umbra not make sense? The Lower Umbra is where things end. The sphere of Entropy manipulates the the integrity of things, people, ideas, etc and can bring them to the end of their cycle. I feel it makes perfect sense. Just as the sphere of Mind can be tied to the High Umbra where ideas begin and Life is tied to the Middle Umbra where idea takes form Entropy is tied to the Lower Umbra where all things end. As for relating Entropy to the Wyrm I think its more of a hold over from Werewolf and how they see it, right or wrong. A Mage normally doesn't make this distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the same reason you don't need Life to interact with the Middle Umbra.<br /> <br /> For all those, you use Spirit.<br /> <br /> Using Mind to deal with the High Umbra (and the Dreaming I may add) is a form of &quot;inderect&quot; contact. Let me try to explain<br /> <br /> First, everything has a spirit right? So, a marble statue has a spirit (that is probably sleeping). But, if I use Matter to turn the state into a computer, the spirit will also change accordinly.<br /> <br /> So, when I create chimeras of the Dreaming using Mind 3, I'm not really dealing with the spiritual substance of dreams, I'm dealing with the psychic energies that are the source of those spiritual manifestations. If I use Spirit 5, I'll shape glamour actively to make the chimera... With Mind, I'm &quot;blowing the sand&quot; to make draws on it, I'm not using a stick for that.<br /> <br /> Mind 4 and 5 Astral projection lets you connect your mind with the collective inconscient, it's an atunement of your thoughts to reach the collective thoughts... The thing is, the collective mind has a manifestation in the Umbra - the High Umbra. It's not the same as steping sideways using Spirit, you're not &quot;entering&quot; the High Umbra using Mind, but rather you let the High Umbra &quot;enter you&quot; (don't forget that your body is still resting in the physical plane).<br /> <br /> I could make a similar case in saying that what you need to deal with the Low Umbra is Prime, based on the same arguments (since Prime deals with creation/destruction).<br /> <br /> Besides... What level of Entropy do you think that fits this? Level 1, that allows you to &quot;see&quot; randomness? Level 2, that allows manipulation of chance? 3 - matter? 4 - life? Or 5 - ideas?<br /> <br /> That whole &quot;tap the energies of the Underworld&quot; doesn't fit to the description of any level (as far as I'm concerned, Entropy doesn't deal with spiritual energies at any level).<br /> <br /> Well, if you think that there is a RANDOM way to make the shroud weaker... By all means, do try. But it would be a very, very odd &quot;coincidente&quot;. Like using Entropy 5, and suddenly a Malfean Onceborn appears &quot; by luck&quot; and weakens it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:02:37-08:00","id":1035394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1035375#post1035375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quote Karlgust:<br /> On the other hand, Entropy should be anatema to the Celestial Chorus... Everything that is, comes from The One, and even that which could seem against The One, only is make his glory even more magnificent... Who do you think you are to interfere with The One's plans? Changing Fate is changing the &amp;quot;God's Plan&amp;quot;, and interfere with God's Plan is the WORSE of the sins...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This of course assumes that a Mage that manipulates the Threads of Fate for himself or another wasn't doing so because it WAS his fate to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be. I just stated a <i>possible</i> view of the Celestial Chorus on it. Being as diverse as they are thou, it's hard to say they would REALLY manage to agree on the subject with that &quot;one&quot; voice that they love so much to tell you about but can never do it themselves. Still, that's one subject I can easily see being the cause of many <b>heated</b> internal discussions among them (the kind of friendly debate that makes mages throw quintessencial energy balls on each other)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:11:52-08:00","id":1035397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1035394#post1035394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could be. I just stated a <i>possible</i> view of the Celestial Chorus on it. Being as diverse as they are thou, it's hard to say they would REALLY manage to agree on the subject with that &quot;one&quot; voice that they love so much to tell you about but can never do it themselves. Still, that's one subject I can easily see being the cause of many <b>heated</b> internal discussions among them (the kind of friendly debate that makes mages throw quintessencial energy balls on each other)</div> </div> </div> </div>Taken from the Revised Celestial Chorus Tradition Book:<br /> <br /> Entropy: The Ends of Existence<br /> Some would call it luck or fate, but to the Chorus, the end or consummation of all things is a matter of divine destiny and providence. The Chorus focuses less on Entropy as the \u201cdeath\u201d Sphere and more on Entropy as the Sphere of divine fortune and blessing. Some Choristers believe that all of reality follows a master script that the One foresaw and constructed long ago. However, one seeress of the Silver moon Clan is said to have asked the One\u2019s angel what her cabal should do, only to have the angel respond \u201csurprise me.\u201d Therefore, she inferred that destiny and fortune are not prescribed scripts, but improvisational theaters wherein the One works with created beings to bless the world. Choristers often call upon revelations or divine emanations to read the process of Entropy. Creation of Entropy \u2014 that is, tearing things down \u2014 stems mostly from rare curses. Such uses of magic are frowned upon, and in truth the Chorus\u2019 structures do not often accommodate such methodologies very well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:15:58-08:00","id":1035401,"title":"","content":"The big problem with Entropy is that it is a bullshit sphere. The effects unrelated to decay and ghosts are all incredibly meta and hard to wrap your head around. Consider the M20 rote &quot;Hypernarrative Influence, Mind 4/Entropy 2&quot;. By using Mind and Entropy you can cause someone's gun to run out of ammo or a car to blow up when shot in the gas tank. Now, in a real world this obviously makes no sense. The number of bullets in a gun and a number of shots made are real static quantities. The only reason you can manipulate them in the game is because they are unknown to you, the player, because to the player most of the universe exists in a quantum state of &quot;undescribed by the GM&quot;. The same goes for using Entropy to catch a cab, using Entropy to win a game of poker, using Entropy to do basically anything bigger than interaction between electrons. This results in Entropy being the ur-Sphere that can do things related to every other sphere while also being coincidental.<br /> <br /> And then there are rotes like Ring of Truth which lets you detect lies with Entropy. Why? I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:24:38-08:00","id":1035410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1035371#post1035371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Look. If you are going to come here and educate us foolish mortals who can not comprehend the concept of Entropy as fully as your magnificent mind can, then you can at least read the goddamn book to make sure you do actually know what you are talking about. Because you know, I can post quotes from Revised book too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>*</u> </b>&amp;quot;Low Umbra&amp;quot; means Underworld.<br /> <br /> <br /> But other than that, I really don't know who you are arguing with. No one in this thread claimed that Entropy and Wyrm are related. No one anywhere has claimed that Entropy &amp;quot;is tainted&amp;quot;. I personally have never played with anyone who tried to hammer Werewolf mythology into Mage, but this can be chalked up to limited sample size. You are tilting at windmills mate. And you are being condescending while doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I sounded like that, it was not my intention. I'm not saying that anything I write are the prestine words of The One written on tables. And I'm open to new ideas. I'm simply exposing mine ideas. If they are wrong, I'll discard them and adopt new ones. I don't know why you felt I'm being condescending, but if you saw that way, I'm honestly not trying to be, I'm just putting what I think on the table.<br /> <br /> About the difference of revised and M20, I simply state they &quot;it seems they gave a <b>bigger</b> emphazis on that &quot;destructive&quot; aspect&quot;. I didnt said there was nothing in the 3ed. <br /> <br /> Besides, there is a <b>HUGE</b> difference from saying worlds like &quot;dissolution&quot; and &quot;breakdown&quot; from using a word like <b>decay</b>, and even more for <b>CORRUPTION</b> . Dissolution and breakdown implies neutral events; but <b>corruption</b> implies some kind of <i>evil intent</i> (not to mention the part about tapping with Low Umbra energies that I also disagree - which by the way, your &quot;explanation&quot; about it being the Underworld just made you guilty of the same sin that you now accuses me of being condescending) . That's what I was refering for<br /> <br /> So, I don't know why you're picking on me about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:30:49-08:00","id":1035416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1035397#post1035397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...The Chorus focuses less on Entropy as the \u201cdeath\u201d Sphere...</div> </div> </div> </div>You see? That's what I'm talking about... Why there are so many correlations between &quot;Entropy&quot; and &quot;Death&quot;? (To the point of saying this is a Sphere for necromancers or nephandi rather than Spirit - not to mention that this is the Sphere of choice for the death cult called Euthanatos).<br /> <br /> Is it only me that gets bothered by this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:41:21-08:00","id":1035425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1035397#post1035397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Taken from the Revised Celestial Chorus Tradition Book:<br /> <br /> Entropy: The Ends of Existence<br /> Some would call it luck or fate, but to the Chorus, the end or consummation of all things is a matter of divine destiny and providence. The Chorus focuses less on Entropy as the \u201cdeath\u201d Sphere and more on Entropy as the Sphere of divine fortune and blessing. Some Choristers believe that all of reality follows a master script that the One foresaw and constructed long ago. However, one seeress of the Silver moon Clan is said to have asked the One\u2019s angel what her cabal should do, only to have the angel respond \u201csurprise me.\u201d Therefore, she inferred that destiny and fortune are not prescribed scripts, but improvisational theaters wherein the One works with created beings to bless the world. Choristers often call upon revelations or divine emanations to read the process of Entropy. Creation of Entropy \u2014 that is, tearing things down \u2014 stems mostly from rare curses. Such uses of magic are frowned upon, and in truth the Chorus\u2019 structures do not often accommodate such methodologies very well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's strange if you think about abhraamic religions, were God knows everything. Imo, if one traditions would believe in Fate and Destiny, that would be the CC.<br /> <br /> And even if we consider that passage... The chorus have so many voices, that I think it would be hard for ALL of them to agree in that.<br /> <br /> In modern age, under the unification attempts, maybe those that revile on Entropy, while still considering it a sin, could agree on &quot;letting the one punish his hubris&quot;, but I still can't see ALL the chorists thinking they can &quot;surprise the one&quot;.<br /> <br /> Imo, Entropy 1 would be not only fine, but <b>recomended</b> (as a way of &quot;trying to understand the will of the One&quot; or trying to graps &quot;God's plan)... Or maybe, even that would not be good for them (the One's plan are a mystery), but anything beyond that I think that at least SOME of them would believe to be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:51:42-08:00","id":1035430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1035401#post1035401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big problem with Entropy is that it is a bullshit sphere. The effects unrelated to decay and ghosts are all incredibly meta and hard to wrap your head around. Consider the M20 rote &amp;quot;Hypernarrative Influence, Mind 4/Entropy 2&amp;quot;. By using Mind and Entropy you can cause someone's gun to run out of ammo or a car to blow up when shot in the gas tank. Now, in a real world this obviously makes no sense. The number of bullets in a gun and a number of shots made are real static quantities. The only reason you can manipulate them in the game is because they are unknown to you, the player, because to the player most of the universe exists in a quantum state of &amp;quot;undescribed by the GM&amp;quot;. The same goes for using Entropy to catch a cab, using Entropy to win a game of poker, using Entropy to do basically anything bigger than interaction between electrons. This results in Entropy being the ur-Sphere that can do things related to every other sphere while also being coincidental.<br /> <br /> And then there are rotes like Ring of Truth which lets you detect lies with Entropy. Why? I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol, now that's a perspective I had never taken in account... And, sadly, I must agree on you on many parts...<br /> <br /> Entropy is a Sphere that works at the players level and not at the characters level LOL<br /> <br /> So... Entropy is so powerful, so powerful... that works in the real world hahaha<br /> <br /> Well... That route you said... What does Mind 4 have to do with it?<br /> <br /> I do have a problem with A LOT of official rotes that the writers seem to have just took random Spheres at random levels out of their asses and just put in there just so they wouldn't need to say that they don't know","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:41:56-08:00","id":1035460,"title":"","content":"It seems to me your biggest issue is with the coralation of Entropy with death and wickedness. Though death easily fits with the sphere of Entropy (death being an end) I've never thought of it as a sphere of wickedness or evil. Nor is it ever implied. <br /> <br /> Heavy users of Entropy are known to suffer from Jhor more often than others but thats not due to Entropy being inherently evil. Heavy use of any sphere for the purposes of killing can lead to Jhor, they arent considered to be associated with evil because of it. Howerver, since Entropy does deal with the end of things it is given power over corruption (which does not always imply evil intent), decay and death. Just because it shares a close relationship wih that which is often considered evil does not make it evil. Entropy is a tool like any other sphere, how it is used is up to the ideals of its wielder.<br /> <br /> As a note I've never considered the Lower Umbra as an ideal of evil either, only as a realm of endings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 01-20-2017, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T18:10:24-08:00","id":1035565,"title":"","content":"I dunno, I'd say all the spheres are tinged with evil if used the right (or wrong) way.<br /> <br /> Mind allows to destroy a persons identity, leaving them as a shell of their former self.<br /> Life can kill with minimal effort, at a much easier rank than Entropy, that goes double for Forces, especialy when dealing with fire.<br /> Then there's Prime, which allows you to literately remove a man from existence.<br /> Time and Corr both have similar capabilities to trap someone outside of space or time potentially forever. Speaking of traping, Matter. The ultimate in &quot;get out of that one&quot; spheres.<br /> And don't get me started on the banes and demons spirit can summon.<br /> <br /> Entropy has a dark side like all the other spheres.<br /> It governs the eventual end point of all things, and that can include things like &quot;blessings&quot; &quot;good luck rituals&quot; &quot;fortune telling&quot; &quot;guidance&quot; and just &quot;pluck&quot;.<br /> <br /> When one does an Entropy effect in my games, I usually have it reflect in lowered difficulties in corresponding die rolls, or in just getting a gut feeling on what they need to do next. The more often they really on this, the more likely the domino effect will get them in the end, and a paradox backlash during an Entropy effect is not going to be a fun time.<br /> <br /> As for things like &quot;ring of truth&quot; I tend to go with the rule of degrees. Few successes means only a vague idea, while more will give a better handle on the lies spoken, if any. However, without Mind, it will be impossible to know what the truth actually is or how much they are hiding behind a well placed truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T18:19:13-08:00","id":1035566,"title":"","content":"Correspondence can kill people more easily than trapping them outside of space. Just teleport them one mile up and let them make their own six foot grave in the concrete when they land. In my games, the primary combat utility for Entropy is to cause the ammunition of the guns of the enemy to explode when they try to shoot the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T18:25:53-08:00","id":1035573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1035566#post1035566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correspondence can kill people more easily than trapping them outside of space. Just teleport them one mile up and let them make their own six foot grave in the concrete when they land. In my games, the primary combat utility for Entropy is to cause the ammunition of the guns of the enemy to explode when they try to shoot the player.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a rote for that using Forces and Corr in the Hermtic Trad book.<br /> <br /> You transform the bullets kinetic energy from from prepelling forward to exploading outward. The Corr is just so you can target the bullet, which is over wise out of sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T18:39:32-08:00","id":1035576,"title":"","content":"A Matter and Correspondence rote could also transform the entire bullet into propellant, which would burst the barrel of the gun, and would cause major problems for the shooter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T10:28:12-08:00","id":1035746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034803-entropy-disambiguation-sphere-also-broken-nomenclature-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1035566#post1035566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correspondence can kill people more easily than trapping them outside of space. Just teleport them one mile up and let them make their own six foot grave in the concrete when they land. In my games, the primary combat utility for Entropy is to cause the ammunition of the guns of the enemy to explode when they try to shoot the player.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just that?<br /> <br /> How about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> Dim Mak (Entropy 1) - add successes on damage rolls (that's RAW, but I just allow for a maximum of 2 extra damage, I don't think it make sense to make an artifact like &quot;the third eye of jade to see all the chakras&quot; to give someone 10 automatic successes in damage rolls just because they saw the enemies cosmus and hit them exactly in their weakest point)<br /> <br /> Begginers Luck (Entropy 2) - add successes on skills rolls<br /> <br /> Minor Curse (Entropy 2) - remove succeses from enemies (your successes on Arete becomes a &quot;1&quot; roll for enemies)<br /> <br /> Malfction on equipaments (Entropy 3) - now, that's for breaking the big bad techies their little precious toys<br /> <br /> Magikal Anvil (Entropy 2 or 3) - the rotted tree behing the big final boss falls on his head, the rooftops falls on your enemies head, the wooden flor in the hunted house you are falls beneath his feet, a cable power on the street breaks and fall on him, turning your enemy in into ashes, a car run over him by &quot;accident&quot; while he is pointing his plasma cannon at you and making his typical villan speech about how he is superior, and so on. Making a flower vase hanging in a window bellow his head fall would require Entropy 2 - that would just manipulate events in your way. To make something break in a way beneficial to you requires Entropy 3.<br /> <br /> Curse the Body (Entropy 4) - not exactly a rote, but a collection of possible effects of my own making - - note that at Entropy 4 you can use this in Vampires (not Werebeasts thou, those still require Spirit 2, and Changellings would need Spirit 2 or Mind 3, that's a matter of debate and it's to to the ST)<br /> <u>Paralysis of a Limb</u> (paralysing an enemy's leg or arm is very useful)<br /> <u>Attribute Burst</u> - althouth you can't increase your physical attributes properly using Entropy (that would need Life), you can improve the effectivness of your body. With that effect, you can improve your damage, physical resistance, reflexes. Maybe your body gets a sudden surge of adrenaline, maybe you're temporalily possessed by a marcial spirit. Even thought you don't gain muscles, your body will be faster, thougher, or stronger. Use succesess to improve physical attributes.<br /> <u>Weaken</u> - take away physical attributes from your enemies. If any reach 0, they can't move<br /> <u>Heart Attack or Brain Aneurism</u> - poof! They're gone! (Warning: won't work on many supernatural)<br /> <br /> <b>Real</b> Dim Mak - every succes gives one extra damage... Like the vampiric Potence (view it as you wish... After you hit the target, the chock wave &quot;disorganize&quot; the enemy tissiues, cells, organs, whatever... Be as it may, it's aditional magikal damage)<br /> <br /> <u>Death Ray</u> or <u>Desintegration Ray</u> - pretty self explanatory; every succes gives 2 dice of Lethal Damage, Aggraveted if you use Prime 2 and 1 Quintessence. Or, you may do exactly the same, but with the <u>Evil Eye</u>: look at your enemy and rejoice on his pain. With another version of this, you just cause him pain, without any damage (the advantage of causing pain is that the target don't get to resist with Vigor if they can; with 7 levels of &quot;pain damage&quot;, the target gets unconscious).<br /> <u>Numbness</u> - go full Chakha of the house of Virgo from the Zodiac Knights; take away the sight, hearing, smell, taste, touch, of the target. Can't take away magical senses (most of the time thou, those senses rely on some assistance from the regular mundane 5 senses).<br /> <br /> And if all else fails...<br /> <br /> Friend or Foe (Entropy 5) - make your enemies shoot one another, instead of shooting YOU. Why would they do that? Well... Who knows? By accident... Or a perception glitch that made they confuse each other with you... Or perhaps, just temporary insanity... Just remember thou, the more unlikely the reason, the more successes needed, and greater the chances of making it a Vulgar effect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 01-21-2017, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T10:41:22-08:00","id":1035754,"title":"","content":"Enrropy 4 deals aggravated damage to living targets on its own. It does not require Prime 2. That is RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T10:49:19-08:00","id":1035756,"title":"","content":"And, with Entropy 1, you can place yourself during combat in a place where your enemies will be exactly bellow the most fragile part of the rooftop, which in turn will allow you to &quot;break&quot; it in their heads without needing as much successes... So:<br /> <br /> Get to Know the Terrain (Entropy 1) - this allows you to know how to best take advantage of your enviroment and how to best position yourself, thus reducing the necessary amount of successes needed for many Effects of Entropy (and others) or feats, up to a maximum of 2. That's very useful for driving at fast speed to try to evade persecutors - just let your guts tell you wich turns to make","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}